Borrowed ideas and API shapes, with credit:

  vercel-labs/ui, "UI SDK" (https://github.com/vercel-labs/ui), Apache-2.0, Copyright Vercel, Inc.
    - The idea of an agent bridge: components register themselves, and an agent reads them
      with `snapshot`, finds them with `query` and drives them with `act`, instead of reading
      a page or accessibility tree and tapping. The tool names and the shape of their input
      (`steps: [{ ref, action, args }]`, `ref` by id or label), the `allow` callback that can
      refuse or wait on a step, a per-element "a person must do this" mark (`data-agent-confirm`
      there, `confirm` here), "hidden" and "secret" marks, and the benchmark's task and
      measures (tool calls, text read, time, tokens, cost) come from UI SDK's agent bridge
      and its agent benchmark.
    - The three tool descriptions in `src/tools.ts` are rewritten for this package; they follow the
      structure of the UI SDK ones. UI SDK targets the DOM (React, Vue, Svelte, Solid, Web
      Components) and does not cover React Native, which is why this package exists.

  Model Context Protocol (https://modelcontextprotocol.io), the JSON-RPC shapes in `src/mcp.ts`.

No source code from vercel-labs/ui is included in this package.
